        // clone(CLONE_VM|CLONE_VFORK|SIGCHLD, 0), measured at 0x4111 coming
        // out of the pinned BusyBox init. Both shapes become the same
        // copy-on-write fork here, which differs from Linux in two ways
        // worth naming: the child gets its own copy of the address space
        // rather than sharing the parent's, and the parent is not suspended
        // until the child execs. Both differences are in the safe
        // direction for a vfork caller -- a caller may not rely on writes
        // reaching the parent, and every one of them execs or _exits
        // immediately -- but a program that reads a value the child wrote
        // would see the pre-fork value here and the child's value on Linux.
