        // pid if it hasn't exited yet, or the last reaped child's pid if
        // it has -- the live child's pid alone would wrongly read back
        // 0 once reaped (has_child cleared), and a fixed
        // literal (this used to be the literal 2, the only pid the old
        // two-process model could ever produce) is wrong for any process
        // other than the original root.
        // GitHub issue #437: a SEARCH, not a comparison. This asked
        // first_child's pid and fell back to the last reaped one, which
        // was exact while a parent could have one child. With several,
        // wait4(pid) for any of them but the newest would have been
        // -EINVAL.
        let selecting: bool = requested_pid != 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF;
        let known_child: bool =
            kernel_process_current_has_child_pid(requested_pid) ||
            (requested_pid != 0 &&
             requested_pid == kernel_process_last_reaped_pid(current_authority));
