        // (kernel_process_is_child() used to gate this to the tree root
        // only) -- kernel_process_current_has_child_pid()/_last_reaped_pid()
        // above are already relative to whichever slot is calling, and
        // kernel/kernel/process.tkb's own child-exit/wait bookkeeping is
        // now per-slot too, so any live process may legitimately wait4()
